 "final_summary": "The bug was caused by case-sensitive validation of the assignee_id filter, which rejected 'None' as invalid. The fix converts the assignee_id value to lowercase when checking for 'none', ensuring that both 'none' and 'None' are correctly interpreted as unassigned tasks. This makes the filter behavior consistent with the expected behavior of returning unassigned tasks.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/query.py b/tracker/query.py\nindex d765032..b7b7d50 100644\n--- a/tracker/query.py\n+++ b/tracker/query.py\n@@ -58,7 +58,7 @@ def build_filters(params, now_iso=None):\n         args.extend(statuses)\n     assignee = params.get(\"assignee_id\")\n     if assignee is not None and assignee != \"\":\n-        if str(assignee) == \"none\":\n+        if str(assignee).lower() == \"none\":\n             clauses.append(\"assignee_id IS NULL\")\n         else:\n             clauses.append(\"assignee_id = ?\")\n",
